  "prompt": "Use case: scientific-educational. Asset type: individual vocabulary images for a Japanese children's shiritori dictionary.\nEDIT TARGET: attached 2048x2048 equal 4 by 4 white grid template. Paint exactly sixteen independent illustrations into its cells, in row-major order, left to right then top to bottom. Preserve the exact canvas size, all cell dimensions, ALL FIVE horizontal and FIVE vertical continuous pure MAGENTA #ff00ff lines INCLUDING the outer frame, their positions, straightness and thickness. Do not erase, cover, move or redraw dividers. Magenta is reserved only for the grid. No extra panels, no captions, labels, letters, numerals, logos or watermarks.\nStyle: clear gentle natural-history picture-book illustration with accurate species anatomy and distinguishing colors. Each complete subject and its shadow stays inside its own cell; use the cell generously, no mandatory large margins. Light neutral background. Never substitute another species or invent variety-specific coloration. Crop must not amputate the subject. For rice cultivars use botanically plausible ordinary green/gold rice panicles and pale grains, with a small plain bowl of cooked white rice only for table-rice cultivars. Sake-rice shows panicle and uncooked rice, without alcohol bottles. Forage-rice shows lush rice stems/leaves, without a cooked-rice bowl. Cultivar illustrations are illustrative examples, never diagnostic identification photographs.\nSixteen subjects in exact order:\n1. アフリカニシキヘビ (Python sebae): アフリカにすむ大型のヘビの仲間の爬虫類。体を巻きつけて獲物を捕まえる。\n2. ビスマルクリングパイソン (Bothrochilus boa): ビスマルク諸島にすむヘビの仲間の爬虫類。若いときは輪のような帯模様が目立つ。\n3. ミルクヘビ (Lampropeltis triangulum): 北アメリカなどにすむヘビの仲間の爬虫類。赤色や黒色などの帯模様を持つものがいる。\n4. カリフォルニアキングヘビ (Lampropeltis californiae): 白っぽい色と黒っぽい色の模様を持つヘビの仲間の爬虫類。北アメリカ西部にすむ。\n5. メキシカンブラックキングスネーク (Lampropeltis nigrita): つやのある黒い体を持つヘビの仲間の爬虫類。メキシコなどにすむ。\n6. ブラックラットスネーク (Pantherophis obsoletus): 北アメリカにすむヘビの仲間の爬虫類。成体は黒っぽい体を持つ。\n7. セイブシシバナヘビ (Heterodon nasicus): 鼻先が上向きに反ったヘビの仲間の爬虫類。北アメリカにすむ。\n8. トウブシシバナヘビ (Heterodon platirhinos): 上に反った鼻先を持つヘビの仲間の爬虫類。北アメリカ東部などにすむ。\n9. ヨーロッパヤマカガシ (Natrix natrix): 首の後ろに淡い模様があるものが多いヘビの仲間の爬虫類。水辺にもすむ。\n10. ヨーロッパクサリヘビ (Vipera berus): 背中にジグザグの模様があるものが多い毒ヘビの仲間の爬虫類。寒い地域にもすむ。\n11. ガボンアダー (Bitis gabonica): 太い体と落ち葉に似た模様を持つ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。アフリカにすむ。\n12. パフアダー (Bitis arietans): 太い体を持つ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。アフリカなどにすむ。\n13. ライノセラスアダー (Bitis nasicornis): 鼻先に角のような突起を持つ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。アフリカの林にすむ。\n14. サハラツノクサリヘビ (Cerastes cerastes): 砂漠にすむ毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。目の上に角のようなうろこがあるものが多い。\n15. サイドワインダー (Crotalus cerastes): 砂の上を横向きに進む動きで知られる毒のあるヘビの仲間の爬虫類。尾に音を出す部分がある。\n16. トウブダイヤガラガラヘビ (Crotalus adamanteus): 背中にひし形の模様が並ぶ大型の毒ヘビの仲間の爬虫類。北アメリカ南東部にすむ。\nAll snakes have a single anatomically continuous body, one head and one tail, no legs, no extra heads. Use natural adult/wild-type colors and morphology for the exact scientific species. No attacking people, bites, wounds or gore. Venomous and nonvenomous species are depicted observationally.\nEDIT OF GENERATED SHEET: first reference is the generated sheet to repair; the template is a geometry reference. Change ONLY cells 2 and 3 in the top row. Cell 2 Bothrochilus boa: show a JUVENILE Bismarck ringed python with vivid ORANGE ground color and broad BLACK encircling rings, a small blackish head. This is NOT a brown ball python with oval spots. Cell 3 Lampropeltis triangulum sensu stricto: show a wild-type EASTERN milk snake, pale gray/cream ground with large REDDISH-BROWN dorsal saddle blotches outlined in BLACK, smaller lateral blotches, smooth scales and a slender head. Do NOT use the generic continuous red-white-black coral-like ring pattern of other milksnake species. Preserve every other cell. Keep all magenta lines, exact 4x4 cell placement and overall canvas; no labels or extra panels.",
